OL,3,GNEWSASafety fears over drought-affected
OL,4,Asports pitches
OL,5,
OL,6,FMonths of hot dry weather have left
OL,7,Fsports pitches in an increasingly
OL,8,Fdangerous state.
OL,10,FFootball, rugby and cricket clubs
OL,11,Facross Wiltshire have expressed fears
OL,12,Fthat the hard ground could lead to
OL,13,Fplayers getting injured.
OL,15,FThe start of the community rugby season
OL,16,Fhas been delayed by the Rugby Football
OL,17,FUnion (RFU), until 21 September instead
OL,18,Fof 5 September, and there are concerns
OL,19,Fthat football leagues may be forced to
OL,20,Fdo the same.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
